# Example fixture: 2x2x2 Si (diamond cubic) supercell (64 atoms) with atom
# #1 substituted to Ge, deliberately left at the ORIGINAL (unrelaxed) Si-Si
# bond distance (2.3655 Ang) -- exactly what a fresh stb-defect substitution
# output looks like before any relaxation. Used to exercise stb-mlrelax's
# default positions-only mode: verified this session that relaxing this
# with MACE-MP-0 moves the Ge-Si bond to 2.4053-2.4093 Ang, squarely in the
# literature range for a dilute substitutional Ge:Si bond (~2.40-2.45 Ang,
# since Ge's covalent radius is larger than Si's).


NumberOfSpecies    2
NumberofAtoms      64

%block ChemicalSpeciesLabel
 1   32   Ge
 2   14   Si
%endblock ChemicalSpeciesLabel

LatticeConstant 1.0 Ang

AtomicCoordinatesFormat  Fractional

%block LatticeVectors
 10.92600000   0.00000000   0.00000000
 0.00000000   10.92600000   0.00000000
 0.00000000   0.00000000   10.92600000
%endblock LatticeVectors

%block AtomicCoordinatesAndAtomicSpecies
